## Random coil and fully folded \(\upbeta\)-sheet reference peptides
Some peptides were synthesised to serve as model of the unfolded and fully folded states. As unfolded reference peptide for CD analysis, we synthesised the full Betanova molecule substituting Gly8 and Gly14 by Ala (Control). Since position L2 of a \(\upbeta\)-turn (Thornton nomenclature)16 occupies an area of the Ramachandran plot that is forbidden to Ala,17 Control should have no propensity to form a \(\upbeta\)-sheet. The typical random coil far-UV CD spectrum displayed by this peptide (Figure 2(a)), its \(\mathrm{H}^{\alpha}\) conformational shift profile (difference between the measured \(\mathrm{H}^{\alpha}\) chemical shifts and the chemical shifts of a random coil reference peptide; see Figure 2(c)) and the absence of any long-range NOE confirmed this. To take into account any sequence-dependent effects on the random coil \(\mathrm{H}^{\alpha}\) and \({}^{1}\mathrm{HN}\) chemical shifts, eight residue peptides identical with the \(\upbeta\)-strands of some of the \(\upbeta\)-sheets were synthesised to serve as appropriate reference values for NMR conformational shifts. A highly stable peptide was required to represent a fully folded \(\upbeta\)-sheet. D-Pro at the first of the two positions of a type I' \(\upbeta\)-turn strongly induces \(\upbeta\)-sheet formation in adjacent strands.18 Therefore, one of the most stable mutants (FLM; see below) was modified to have D-Pro instead of Asn at position L1 of both \(\upbeta\)-turns. The \(\upbeta\)-sheet far-UV CD spectrum (Figure 2(b)) and NMR analysis of this peptide (\(^{\mathrm{D}}\mathrm{FLM}\)) in \(40\%\) (v/v) aqueous methanol revealed a very high population of \(\upbeta\)-sheet structure. In fact, the RMS deviation of the \(\mathrm{H}^{\alpha}\) conformational shifts (\(\mathrm{RMS}\Delta\delta_{\mathrm{Hz}}\))19 for the \(\upbeta\)-strand residues of \({}^{\mathrm{D}}\mathrm{FLM}\) (\(\mathrm{RMS}\Delta\delta_{\mathrm{Hz}}=+0.42\)) is very similar to the averaged \(\Delta\delta_{\mathrm{Hz}}\) value observed in \(\upbeta\)-sheet proteins (\(\Delta\delta_{\mathrm{Hz}}=+0.40\ \mathrm{ppm}\))20 (see the \(\mathrm{H}^{\alpha}\) conformational shift profile in Figure 2(c)). This, together with the CD spectrum, the protein-like NMR spectral dispersion and the large number of long-range NOEs detected for this peptide, indicates that the \(\upbeta\)-sheet population for \({}^{\mathrm{D}}\mathrm{FLM}\) is close to \(100\%\). A detailed NMR conformational study of this peptide will be reported elsewhere. On the basis of these results, we used \({}^{\mathrm{D}}\mathrm{FLM}\) in aqueous methanol as reference peptide of the folded state of Betanova's mutants. All reference peptides are shown in Scheme 2 (mutations are underscored; ac, acetylated; am, amidated):
